---
title: Chili crisp garlic noodles
servings: 2
tags: [chinese, quick]
cuisine: chinese
source: Chilli Crisp Noodles by Nagi Maehashi, RecipeTin Eats, https://www.recipetineats.com/chilli-crisp-noodles/
---

Whisk the @Chinese sesame paste{2%tbsp}, @light soy sauce{2%tbsp},
@rice vinegar{1%tbsp}, @sugar{1%tsp}, @toasted sesame oil{2%tsp} and
@kosher salt{1/8%tsp} in a bowl big enough to toss the noodles in. Scatter the
@scallions{1}(finely sliced) on top without stirring.

Warm the @chili crisp{2%tbsp}(heaped, with its oil) in a #small pan{} over
medium heat. Add the @ginger{1%tbsp}(finely minced) and
@garlic{1%tbsp}(finely minced) and stir ~{30%seconds}, until golden. Pour it
straight over the scallions so they sizzle.

Boil the @ramen noodles{140%g}(instant, 2 cakes; or 250 g fresh lo mein) as the
packet says, about ~{2%minutes} for ramen.

Lift the noodles straight into the bowl with a little of their water and toss
until coated. Stir in the @?cilantro{1/3%cup}(roughly chopped), then taste and
add salt or more chili crisp.

> Chili crisps vary a lot in heat; taste yours and start with less if it is
> fierce.
